    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d976">

                <pb facs="1061" n="1049" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg1049"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/9–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Mr. Alexander C. Kirk, Political Adviser
                        to the Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean Theater, at Caserta</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-07T20:00:00-04:00">September 7,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>814. Dept has discussed Naf 1069 and 1070 [<hi rendition="#italic">1071</hi>]
                    with War Dept (urtel 3512, Sept. 4<anchor n="54" xml:id="d976-f1"/> and Rome’s
                    2527 [<hi rendition="#italic">2572</hi>], Sept. 4) and has requested that CCS
                    reply be expedited so as not to delay return of provinces to Ital
                    administration. As regards Udine, it is expected that CCS will approve retention
                    under AMG only of that part of province necessary for military movements and
                    will recommend public statement of reasons for AMG retention. It is noted from
                    urtel 3540, Sept. 6, that this arrangement would be agreeable to SAC.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
